Phase 1: Proposal & Design

Define problem statement, motivation, objectives, and scope
Identify target users and expected outcomes
Design system architecture (interface → application logic → analysis → data structures → file I/O)
Select and justify core data structures: linked list (timeline), hash table (ID/IP lookup), stack (undo history)
Design class structure: Event, EventList, HashTable, ActionStack, RiskAnalyzer, ReportGenerator, Incident, Investigator
Prepare sample log files (normal + attack-pattern scenarios)
Deliverable: Project proposal document + architecture diagram



Phase 2: Development

Implement Event class and file-parsing logic (LogReader)
Build custom linked list for chronological event storage
Build custom hash table with chaining for Event ID / IP lookup
Implement stack-based undo for investigator actions
Develop RiskAnalyzer for suspicious sequence detection and risk scoring
Build menu-driven console interface (main.cpp)
Set up GitHub repository, version control, and team collaboration workflow
Deliverable: Working prototype with core features functional



Phase 3: Final Implementation

Integrate all modules into a complete end-to-end system
Implement ReportGenerator for structured investigation reports
Test against multiple sample logs (edge cases: malformed lines, unknown IPs, no suspicious activity)
Refine risk-scoring logic and fix bugs identified during testing
Finalize documentation: README, code comments, user guide
Prepare final report and research paper
Deliverable: Complete, tested CyberTrace application + final documentation
